Group 3 -  Final Review and Decision Team (FRDT)
 Member 1 (Senior Oncologist (Lead)): Provides overarching expertise and clinical guidance on treatment decisions, synthesizing data from the previous teams to recommend a treatment plan tailored to the patient.
 Member 2 (Clinical Trial Specialist): Coordinates the clinical trial information and outcomes, ensuring that insights from the ongoing Phase 3 trial are integrated into the treatment decision process and discussing implications for FDA approval.
 Member 3 (Palliative Care Specialist): Ensures that the patient's quality of life is considered in treatment decisions, addressing concerns about potential adverse effects and supporting pain management and symptom relief alongside the novel treatment.


